<title>BELGIUM: Olive oil report further delayed.</title>
<headline>Olive oil report further delayed.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A report on the future of the olive oil regime, due to be adopted by the European Commission on Wednesday, will again be delayed, Commission officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Portuguese Commissioner Joao de Deus Pinheiro, who is absent this week, is expected to invoke Article 4 of Commission rules to postpone discussion.</p>
<p>The following week Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler is visiting Australia.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission is likely to discuss the report on February 12,&quot; said a Commission official.</p>
<p>The report, which had been scheduled in October 1996, has been postponed several times due to opposition from southern olive oil producing countries who fear it will result in reforms and a loss of revenue for farmers.</p>
